  "body": "Adds two start options. `--no-activate` creates the window inactive and skips `focus_window()`. `--minimized` also minimizes the window at once.\n\nCause: winit shows a visible, active window with `SW_SHOW`, and the shell called `focus_window()`.\n\nReadings (Windows 11, release build, polled with EnumWindows/GetForegroundWindow, launched from a terminal and from Task Scheduler):\n- `--no-activate`: never the foreground window, also when the project finished loading.\n- `--minimized`: minimized (`IsIconic`) from the first time it is visible; never the foreground window.\n\n## Testing\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base main` on this head, with `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=4`: 10 steps, 0 failed. `ui suites: lib`: 1479 passed. The 8 integration suites passed.\n\nRun by name with `cargo xtask gate test <name> --crate camcraft-ui --exact`, all ok:\n- `start_mode_flags_are_read_and_minimized_implies_no_activate`\n- `default_start_activates_and_shows`\n- `no_activate_shows_without_the_focus`\n- `minimized_creates_an_inactive_window`\n- `each_table_option_is_accepted_by_the_parser`\n- `help_names_each_option_and_variable_of_the_table`\n\nTwo runs with the default job count (16) were red:\n- The `ui build (--no-run)` step failed with \"found invalid metadata files\" for a dependency crate (`png`, then `accesskit`). This looks like a build-cache problem on this machine. It did not repeat with 4 jobs.\n- `ui suites: lib` ended with STATUS_ACCESS_VIOLATION. This crash also happens on plain `main`, without this PR: 8 of 15 runs of `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib` on Windows 11 ended with it. It stops at a random test each time. This PR does not cause it. The one run with 4 jobs did not crash, so a full green lib run is one sample only.\n\nNot exercised: clippy (not installed here), macOS, Linux (Wayland ignores `with_active`), the other gate tiers.\n\nChangelog: Start options `--no-activate` and `--minimized` open the window without taking the focus.\nFixes #3582\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
